    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0044" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/3–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-03-19T12:00:00-05:00">March 19, 1948—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>418. For Clark from Butterworth. CNO<anchor n="76" xml:id="d39-f1"/> Navy Dept
                    states no ammo in Pacific surplus essential war reserves and to draw from such
                    reserves would require action by JCS<anchor n="77" xml:id="d39-f2"/> and
                    National Security Council. CNO therefore believes suggested action (Embtel 445,
                    Mar 11) impracticable. [Butterworth.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thorp</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d39-f1" n="76" xml:id="d39-f1-content">
                <p>Chief of Naval Operations, Adm. Louis E. Denfeld.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d39-f2" n="77" xml:id="d39-f2-content">
